#!/bin/bash
# land-routine-sheet.sh — the routine becomes a sheet: an AM & PM masthead, the
# day in two columns with a photograph and a price against every step, and a bag
# for the whole thing.
#
# PRECONDITIONS, in this order:
#   land-three-photos.sh, land-one-routine.sh   (this tree's Routine.tsx)
#   land-real-shelf.sh                          (the fields this page reads)
#
# FRONTEND ONLY (together-city-react). Push, and Vercel ships it.
set -euo pipefail

cd "$(dirname "$0")"
[ -d together-city-react ] || { echo "!! Run this from the Together-Ai repo root."; exit 1; }

if [ -f .git/index.lock ] && [ ! -s .git/index.lock ]; then
  echo "== clearing a stale empty .git/index.lock"
  rm -f .git/index.lock
fi

NEEDS="The routine is a sheet, not a settings screen"
LOG="$(git log --oneline -40)"
case "$LOG" in
  *"$NEEDS"*) echo "== \"$NEEDS\" is already here. Nothing to do."; exit 0 ;;
esac
case "$LOG" in
  *"One question, one answer, on the tab named after it"*) ;;
  *) echo "!! Run land-one-routine.sh first — this is written against the tree it produces."; exit 1 ;;
esac
case "$LOG" in
  *"A shelf you can buy from"*) ;;
  *) echo "!! Run land-real-shelf.sh first — this page reads fields it adds."; exit 1 ;;
esac

ALLOWED='^ M together-city-react/(public/assets/img/(apple-touch-icon-180|tc-icon-1024|tc-icon-192|tc-icon-512|tc-icon-maskable-512)\.png|public/downloads/TogetherCity\.apk)$'
DIRTY="$(git status --porcelain \
  | grep -Ev '^\?\? (land-.*\.sh|push-.*\.sh|.*\.patch)$' \
  | grep -Ev "$ALLOWED" || true)"
if [ -n "$DIRTY" ]; then
  echo "!! The tree carries changes this script did not expect:"; echo "$DIRTY"; exit 1
fi

PATCH="$(mktemp "${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/land.XXXXXX")"
trap 'rm -f "$PATCH"' EXIT
cat <<'B64EOF' | tr -d '\n' | openssl base64 -d -A > "$PATCH"

B64EOF
WANT="c7442b2cc5f70ffc9c9ea173f2ea075fc3ed888873c8141c5b35c657d4e410a7"
GOT="$(shasum -a 256 "$PATCH" | awk '{print $1}')"
[ "$GOT" = "$WANT" ] || { echo "!! Patch is corrupt."; echo "   want $WANT"; echo "   got  $GOT"; exit 1; }
echo "== patch verified"
git apply --check -C1 "$PATCH" || { echo "!! Patch does not apply cleanly. Nothing written."; exit 1; }
git apply -C1 "$PATCH"
echo "== applied"

cd together-city-react
npx tsc --noEmit
npx vitest run
node scripts/a11y-audit.mjs
node scripts/motion-ceiling.mjs
node scripts/lint-ceiling.mjs
npx vite build
cd ..

git add together-city-react/src/features/beauty/pages/Routine.tsx \
        together-city-react/src/features/beauty/api.ts \
        together-city-react/src/styles/layout.css \
        together-city-react/src/app/relief.spec.ts
git commit -F - <<'MSG'
The routine is a sheet, not a settings screen

The owner sent a reference: an editorial AM & PM skincare sheet, two columns
abreast, a photograph and a price against every step, and a basket for the
whole thing. What was there was correct and unreadable — three stacked cards of
numbered rows at one weight, prices you would not notice, and no way to buy any
of it without leaving for the Market.

WHAT IS THE REFERENCE'S AND WHAT IS NOT, said out loud because the difference
was deliberate rather than a shortfall:

  TAKEN — the masthead, the two columns, the numbered rows with a picture and a
  price, the basket for the whole routine, the assurance strip along the foot.

  NOT TAKEN — its cream ground and bronze rule. Beauty's accent is the city's
  plum and its ground is the city's paper. A hub re-grounding itself is a
  decision for tokens.css; five have earned it and this would be a sixth
  because of one picture. The masthead sits on `--accent-soft`, which is the
  hub's own blush, and gets the warmth without the argument.

  NOT TAKEN — "You save ₹1,225". There is no MRP anywhere in the catalogue, so
  that figure could only have been invented. The total is real and stands on
  its own.

FOUR BANDS, NOT TWO. Morning and evening abreast as in the reference; weekly
and body full width beneath. The reference has nowhere for a wash day or a hand
cream, and the shelf has seventeen hair products and fifteen body ones —
dropping them to match a picture would be redesigning the product to fit the
mock.

THE BAG IS KEYED BY PRODUCT, NOT BY STEP, and that is the one thing here that
would have been a real defect. A cleanser is in the morning band and the
evening band and it is ONE BOTTLE. A bag built per step would have sold this
person two of everything they use twice a day, charged for it, and looked
entirely reasonable doing it. "Add all to bag" walks the deduplicated list, and
the masthead's total is the price of the products, not the sum of the steps.

Checkout is the Market's — the same PaymentSheet, the same wallet, the same
`placeOrder`, which prices every line from the shelf and ignores whatever the
client claims. Nothing new was built to take money.

EVERY STEP LINKS OUT TO WHERE IT IS SOLD. A routine that names a product you
then have to go and search for is homework.

THE PICTURE FALLS THROUGH TWICE. It is hotlinked to a retailer's CDN, which
makes it the least reliable thing on the page; the catalogue carries a second
from a different retailer, and the tile walks primary → alternate → a category
mark. A page full of broken frames reads as a routine that is wrong, which is
far more expensive than a missing photograph.

THREE RULES WENT INTO layout.css AND THE REST STAYED INLINE, each for its own
reason: the serif because relief.spec grants the press's face BY SELECTOR and
cannot see an inline style; the two-column day because it needs a breakpoint
and a divider drawn between the columns rather than around them; the assurance
strip because it is a four-up that becomes a two-up on a phone.

THE DISPLAY SERIF NOW HAS A THIRD BORROWER, and that is a change to a guarded
rule rather than a bit of styling. relief.spec assertion 4 permits exactly one
selector outside the nutrition press to read `--press-serif` and fails on
anything else. `.routine-display` joins `.letter-title` and the archive's
titles in that one selector — one rule, three places, so they cannot drift —
with its reason recorded beside the other two: this masthead is the hub's one
editorial title, and the reference's whole character is this face against the
sans.

The divider between morning and evening is the only rule on the page. It is
what makes them read as two halves of one day rather than two lists that happen
to be adjacent, and it is drawn on the second column so it never appears above
or below anything once they stack at 860px.

tsc clean, vitest green (59 files), a11y 0 at the ceiling, motion and lint at
theirs, vite build clean. Rendered at 960 and 390.

MSG
echo "== committed"

echo
echo "==============================================================="
echo " Landed: $NEEDS"
echo " AM & PM abreast, weekly and body beneath, a bag for the lot."
echo " Push, and Vercel ships it."
echo "==============================================================="
